From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:45:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ieframe: browser service, travel log, window list, script
 helper (3252)

IBrowserService, IDocObjectService and IShellUIHelper2 members that were
stubs now do what Microsoft documents:

- flags, navigate state, code page, title (fires TitleChange), referrer,
  history object (fails when one is set), control windows (status bar,
  toolbar, full screen), palette (none), browser index, parent site, OLE
  object, UpdateBackForwardState, OnHttpEquiv (Exec on the container),
  DisplayParseError (container message or message box).
- pidls: file addresses use shell pidls, other addresses a private pidl
  that only ieframe reads, for IEParseDisplayName, IEGetDisplayName,
  GetPidl, NavigateToPidl, NotifyRedirect.
- GetTravelLog returns a real ITravelLog and ITravelEntry over the host's
  log (CountEntries, Travel, GetTravelEntry, FindTravelEntry, menus,
  Clone), so history.length and history.go work in mshtml. The log kept
  overwriting the address of an entry found again and its first slots
  were not cleared; both fixed, as was a write past the end of the log.
- RegisterWindow/UpdateWindowList use IShellWindows.
- FireDownloadBegin/Complete, GetPendingUrl, GetUrlSearchComponent,
  ActiveElementChanged, HideUI.
- ShellUIHelper: NavigateAndFind (selects the text once loaded),
  AddDesktopComponent, ShowBrowserUI; AutoScan and UpdateDesktopComponent
  stay E_NOTIMPL as documented.

